      "quote_britannica": "He died in the year of the week SSS, and was faceded by Sandoshina.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "After his death."
    },
    {
      "point": "Identity of the person described.",
      "quote_britannica": "Elarhaddon, in the opinion of Sir Ilane Newton, seems to be the Shanghai who often, as Catecharina fayo, old way after the result of Syria, the name Bekriamo polar being derived from Afrhadon Pal.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "Esarhaddon, also spelled Essarhaddon, Assarhaddon and Ashurhaddon (Neo-Assyrian Akkadian: 𒀭𒊹𒉽𒀸, also 𒀭𒊹𒉽𒋧𒈾 Aššur-aḫa-iddina, meaning \" Ashur has given me a brother\";"
    }
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Esarhaddon was the son of Sennacherib.",
      "tag": "enduring",
      "quote_britannica": "ESARHADDON, the fen of Sennacherib, and his favorite in the Baylorion of Alfryen.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "murdered their father in 681 and planned to seize the Neo-Assyrian throne."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Esarhaddon reigned for 13 years at Babylon.",
