    },
    {
      "old": "Shanghai",
      "new": "king",
      "quote_britannica": "Elarhaddon, in the opinion of Sir Ilane Newton, seems to be the Shanghai who often, as Catecharina fayo,",
      "quote_wikipedia": "was the king of the Neo-Assyrian Empire from 681 to 669 BC."
    }
  ],
  "wiki_only_topics": [
    {
      "topic": "Conquest of Egypt",
      "quote_wikipedia": "Esarhaddon is most famous for his conquest of Egypt in 671 BC, which made his empire the largest the world had ever seen,"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Civil war and ascent to the throne",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The murder, and Arda-Mulissu's aspirations of becoming king himself, made Esarhaddon's rise to the throne difficult, and he first had to defeat his brothers in a six-week-long civil war."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Paranoia and security measures",
      "quote_wikipedia": "His brothers' attempted coup had been unexpected and troublesome for Esarhaddon, and he would be plagued by paranoia and mistrust for his officials, governors and male family members until the end of his reign."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Influence of female relatives",
      "quote_wikipedia": "Also perhaps resulting from his mistrust for his male relatives, Esarhaddon's female relatives, such as his mother Naqiʾa and his daughter Šērūʾa-ēṭirat, were allowed to wield considerably more influence and political power during his reign than women had been allowed in any previous period of Assyrian history,"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Military campaigns in various regions",
      "quote_wikipedia": "successfully campaigned in Media, Persia, Elam, the Arabian Peninsula, Anatolia, the Caucasus, and the Levant, defeated the Kushite Empire and conquered Egypt and Libya,"
    }
  ]
